    "result_text": "Sheet-wide claim numbering now restarts each fiscal year. When a claim is opened and period numbering isn't in force, it gets `FY<year>-<n>`. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec; I didn't rerun it after my last edit, which only changed a comment.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Which fiscal year:** it's taken from the claim's due-by date, the same date that places a claim in a period. It uses the fiscal-start-month of the sheet the claim is opened on. The year is named after the calendar year it starts in, the same way the \"generate fiscal year\" periods are named. If a claim has no due-by, its own date is used.\n- **Shared across the tree:** each fiscal year has one counter shared by every sheet in the tree. It starts at 1 for the year's first numbered claim anywhere in the tree, and each new claim takes the next number after the highest given on any sheet. The top sheet of the tree stays locked while a number is taken, so two claims never get the same number.\n- **Unchanged behaviour:** numbers already given (the plain 1, 2, \u2026) stay as they are. Per-period numbering (`<period>-<n>`, `X-<n>`) still wins when it's in force.\n- **Everything else that numbers claims** (opening, splitting, reassigning, transfer and clone) goes through the same function, so it all follows the new rule.\n\n**What changed**\n- `SheetService.nextFiscalYearNumber` replaces `nextClaimNumber`, which nothing else used.\n- `SheetRepository` has two new queries for the counter.\n- `ClaimService.nextNumber` and a new `fiscalYearOf` work out the number and the year.\n- I updated the doc comments in `Claim.java` and `claims-api.ts`. The front end's claim-number pattern already accepted `FY2026-2` as a correction reference, so it needed no change.\n\n**Things to know**\n- I added no migration. The per-year counters are stored in the existing `claim_number_sequence` table under keys like `fy:2026`, alongside the per-period ones.\n- The old `claim_numbers_used` column on the sheet table is now never written. I left it in place, so the numbers already given are still recorded.\n- Several comments and the settings error message still say \"sheet-wide numbering\" for when period numbering is off. They're slightly out of date but not wrong, and I didn't reword them.",
